      "message": "nit. Not too strong of a preference, but personally, I think that instead of parameterizing like this, it would be a bit better to move the `Test` into a helper function and then explicitly name each case here (like the comments), using the helper to do the same work. It would make it a bit easier to identify failure cases and also to add suppressions in the future if necessary. The only thing that I think would make sense to parameterize would be maybe the `ComputePipeline`/`RenderePipeline`/`RenderBundle` part. \n\nExample:\n```\nvoid ImmediateDataRequiredTest::TestImmediateDataValidation(...) {...}\n\nTEST_F(ImmediateDataRequiredTest, ValidateMissingFrontHalf) {\n    TestImmediateDataValidation(\"mainMiddle\", {{16, 16}}, false);\n}\n\nTEST_F(ImmediateDataRequiredTest, ValidateNominal) {\n    TestImmediateDataValidation(\"mainMiddle\", {{0, 32}}, true);\n}\n\n...\n```",
